// spec: LEX-023, LEX-029
//
// ⚠️ A defect is a statement about the INTERPRETER and is never compiled.
//
// LEX-029 makes '''' the Char holding a quote: one character of VALUE, however
// many of source.  It is a String of length one instead, because LEX-023 was
// measuring the source span.
//
// ⚠️ Three consequences, and the second is the one that settles it: the same
// character carries two types depending on how it is spelled, is not equal to
// itself across those spellings, and has an ordinal under one spelling only.
//
// The expected output is true, true, true, 39 -- and Ord succeeding is part of
// it, which is why that line is last.

WriteLn ('''' is Char);
WriteLn (#39 is Char);
WriteLn ('''' = #39);
WriteLn (Ord (''''));
